###########
  ASBICO
###########

the ASCII-to-BINARY converter for the PSION Series 3


This archive should contain the following files:

ASBICO.OPL	The german OPL Source
ASBICO.OPA	The german Application

ASBICO.PIC	The ICON file
ASBICO.DOC	The file you read now..

ASBICOE.OPL	The english OPL source
ASBICOE.OPA	The englisch Application.


The intention for writting this program was to have a utility to
distribute files for the Series 3 via Echomail on electronic
networks. We will use this utility in the very near future to
present you some software for the Series 3 in the PSION echo on
FIDO net, USENET and other systems.

The converter is written in OPL/g because for a first start up you
need a little OPL program, which everybody can translate.
The startup-program is the file  ASCBIN, an fundamental ASCII-to-
Binary converter.

Transmit the ASCBIN listing via 3LINK interface into your Series 3
and translate it with the OPL editor. Then you can use it to
translate an following ASCII dump, which contains the final and
comfortable ASCBICO converter.

The programm, called ASBICO is an OPL application which can
convert the ASCII to BINARY as well as the BINARY to ASCII.
For a simple error detection, an checksum is calculated.
The path and filename in the first line of the ASCII dump will be
used for the binary output.
If you want an other filename or path, you should edit the first
line of the ASCII dump.

IMPORTANT Notes:
Do not remove the asterix, because they are used to detect the
beginning and the end of the file.
The ASCII dump file on the Series 3 MUST have the extension *.ASC
because ASBICO is looking for this extension.

The utility ASBICO is written by Steffen Penne.

